    "Score combining sleep duration (~30%), efficiency (~30%) and balance of sleep stages (~40%). Optimal range: 7–9h with at least 85% efficiency and 15–20% deep sleep + 20–25% REM (Hirshkowitz et al., 2015).": {
      "comment": "Sleep calculation explanation",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Score combining sleep duration (~30%), efficiency (~30%) and balance of sleep stages (~40%). Optimal range: 7–9h with at least 85% efficiency and 15–20% deep sleep + 20–25% REM (Hirshkowitz et al., 2015)."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Score combinant la durée du sommeil (~30 %), l'efficacité (~30 %) et l'équilibre des stades de sommeil (~40 %). Plage optimale : 7–9 h avec au moins 85 % d'efficacité et 15–20 % de sommeil profond + 20–25 % de REM (Hirshkowitz et al., 2015)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Scoring uses personal baseline deviation (z-score) when enough data is available. A normal day at your baseline scores approximately 50%.": {
      "comment": "Readiness baseline explanation",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Scoring uses personal baseline deviation (z-score) when enough data is available. A normal day at your baseline scores approximately 50%."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Le scoring utilise la déviation par rapport à ta référence personnelle (z-score) lorsque suffisamment de données sont disponibles. Une journée normale à ta référence obtient environ 50 %."
          }
        }
      }
    },
